WEBVTT

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:08.490
Stepping out on
an ordinary Sunday

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:14.990
Stepping out!
A miracle's gonna happen

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.830
It's my day!

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:27.410
Maybe I'll throw off my pajamas

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:34.810
and head out to see her right now

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:42.190
I always turned my eyes away,
thinking she'd hate me

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:49.590
Now I'm saying goodbye
to that negative attitude

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:55.370
My favorite shoes
will always take me

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:02.510
To a place where I'll be happy

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:10.010
It's not someone else
I want to embrace

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:16.150
But a version of
myself that's not fake

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.220
I just want to walk

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.760
Not on tip-toe

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:26.730
Not downcast, either

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:35.640
Just I'm stepping out
on an ordinary Sunday

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:42.080
Stepping out!
Making a little try, try, try

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.350
It's my day!

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:26.520
<i>Rui Hanazawa is in my arms.</i>

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.520
<i>I've yearned for him for so long.</i>

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:31.930
<i>And no matter how cold he was to me...</i>

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:34.570
<i>...I couldn't turn away from him.</i>

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:45.720
<i>If he even smiled a little at me
during those hellish days...</i>

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.240
<i>...I was able to forget my pain.</i>

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:52.110
<i>To think that that very
Rui Hanazawa is in my arms...</i>

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:05.120
"Night of Betrayal"

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.280
I was living with Shizuka in Paris.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:38.300
Her expression when I suddenly
showed up at her apartment...

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.690
...I'll never forget it.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:46.900
<i>Rui!</i>

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:56.260
It was the first time in my life...

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.280
that every single day was filled
with happiness.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:07.160
We talked deep into the night
about when we were kids.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:14.830
And we strolled the streets
of Paris without care.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.510
Oh, and we even talked about you.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:39.850
About me?

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:45.000
Yeah, Shizuka said that
she really liked you, Makino.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.000
<i>Shizuka...</i>

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:57.010
But... those happy days
were short-lived.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.270
Shizuka started college again.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:03.860
During the day she went to school...

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.590
and at night she worked as
a secretary to a lawyer.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:08.840
<i>Bye, Rui. I'm going.</i>

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.840
From the time the door closed
until it opened again...

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.260
I twiddled my thumbs alone.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:32.510
I thought of the time you
first told Tsukasa off.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.010
Me?

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:37.090
<i>You walk around
like big shots...</i>

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:39.410
<i>but you're all protected
by your fathers' names.</i>

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:41.730
<i>You've never worked
for your money.</i>

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.510
<i>So quit mouthing off!</i>

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:50.500
It was true. I realized that
once I left our school...

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.160
...I was completely helpless.

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:57.170
Did you know that, long ago...

00:05:57.170 --> 00:06:00.060
...I was a severely introverted
problem child?

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:02.540
Huh? Oh... yeah...

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.980
I'm still the same...

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:13.210
...A kid who can't do anything
for the woman that I love.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:21.180
I'm sorry.

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:25.350
Why did I tell you all of this?

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:32.010
I wonder why I always end up
talking to you...

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:33.630
...about stuff like this...

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.640
Things that I can't even tell my friends.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:50.420
M-my pager!

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:52.830
Y-yikes. How do I turn this thing off?

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:53.740
Give it to me.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.210
"Come back. Where are you?"

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:00.050
<i>Oh, no. I forgot!</i>

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:01.670
He's worried about you.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:03.950
I have to go back.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:05.760
What about you?

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:07.990
I'm going to stay here.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:09.930
But...

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:11.930
I'm fine now.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:17.680
Makino...

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:21.510
Thanks.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:35.150
<i>What is this feeling?</i>

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:41.190
<i>I wish I could have stayed 
with Rui Hanazawa longer.</i>

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:51.150
Where the hell were you?!

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.900
Oh, my. The gang's all here.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.360
Not, "oh, my." Where were you?

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.580
I-I couldn't sleep, so...

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.360
Er... I went for a walk by myself.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:08.870
<i>Oh, no... I lied.</i>

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:12.990
That's why we told you
not to worry!

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.420
This guy is something else.

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:20.230
He storms into our rooms and
screams that you're missing.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:24.350
He panicked thinking that a wave
washed you away. It was pathetic.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:27.670
Hey! She doesn't have to know that!

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:33.710
Well, we've got an early morning.
Let's hit the hay.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:36.610
We were until you 
woke us up, you jerk!

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:40.310
Domyoji!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.330
Sorry.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.840
At least leave a note
next time, will ya?

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:53.290
Never mind. Let's go to bed.

00:08:58.770 --> 00:08:59.970
<i>That's not what happened.</i>

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:01.850
<i>It's not true.</i>

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:16.680
<i>I held Rui Hanazawa in
my arms at the beach.</i>

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.950
<i>I couldn't walk away.</i>

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:21.020
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:27.550
Here I go!

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:28.490
Yah!

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:30.080
Sojiro!

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:30.930
Got it!

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:40.930
Yes!!

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.440
Wow! Cool!

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:45.880
Sheesh! And this is the plainest one
they had?

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:48.030
That's why I hate designer clothing.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:49.440
Damn!

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.740
I won't let you guys score again!

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:53.720
Don't say that until after...

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:55.840
...you score!

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:58.640
Tsukasa!

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:12.220
They are sooo cool!

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:15.410
And we get to see these four
play volleyball... yummy!

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:18.660
<i>It's true... they do look cool.</i>

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:21.280
Why don't you girls come
and play, too?

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:24.820
What? We don't want to
get a tan, so we'll pass...

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:26.000
Right?!

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:26.940
I'm in.

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.070
You gotta have some fun.

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.920
Look how blue the skies are.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:33.500
What's she getting all
riled up about?

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:35.960
Hey, let it go, Sojiro.

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:39.450
She'll trip you up, so I'm all for it.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:42.450
I heard that! Come on! Let's go!

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:45.100
Okay. But I won't show you
any mercy!

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:47.170
I was hoping you'd say that.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:51.960
Yah!

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:53.210
Makino!

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:54.240
Got it!

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:00.810
Whoa.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.220
Yeah!

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.440
Wow, you go, girl!

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:07.440
You know it.

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:10.060
Cool! Makino!

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.790
Hey, Rui. We're not going
to take this.

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:17.560
Yeah.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.420
All right, let's plan.

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:20.400
Plan?

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:26.490
Huh? Hey, you dropped something.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:27.370
Huh?

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:36.550
She forgot that last night, when
we were talking on the beach.

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.650
Can you give it to
Makino for me?

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:40.790
On the beach?

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:45.090
<i>Er... I went for a walk by myself...</i>

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:48.880
Hey! Hurry up with the ball.
What are you doing?

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:50.130
Rui!

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:34.870
<i>Last night, when we were talking
on the beach...</i>

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:38.870
<i>I was taking a walk by myself.</i>

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:42.680
<i>I was taking a walk by myself.</i>

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:47.380
<i>I was taking a walk by myself.</i>

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:48.550
Tsukasa!

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:54.460
Huh?

00:12:58.160 --> 00:12:59.420
Oh!

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:04.260
Tsukasa!

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.400
Are you okay?

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:09.140
What were you doing, just standing
there in a daze?

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:11.070
Maybe the heat has gotten to him.

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:13.080
Are you okay, Domyoji?

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:17.850
You had us worried.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.220
I'll bring something cold
for you to drink.

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:31.630
Tsukasa, you should take
your time getting up.

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:36.620
Tsukasa is okay. Let's take a dip!

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:37.500
Yay!

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:39.860
Rui!

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:40.700
What?

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:43.140
Are you two...

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:47.410
What?

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:50.940
No, never mind.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:09.200
You can go play on the beach, too.

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:11.600
No, I'm okay here.

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:14.380
I wanted to apologize for
what happened earlier.

00:14:14.380 --> 00:14:15.970
Are you really okay?

00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:16.970
Yeah.

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:21.810
It's really hot here.

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:25.280
But it's not sticky and humid
like Tokyo. It's great!

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:36.150
Makino.

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:37.660
What?

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:41.850
Where's your pager?

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:43.570
Huh? My pager?

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:45.400
<i>Oh, no...</i>

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:53.000
<i>I had it then...</i>

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:00.880
<i>I must have dropped it somewhere.</i>

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:11.660
<i>But if he finds out that I was with
Rui Hanazawa on the beach late at night...</i>

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:15.460
I-It's...

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:17.330
...back at the room.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.020
It suddenly went off when I was
walking on the beach last night.

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:23.470
It caught me by surprise!

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:33.550
What's that?

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:35.550
What's that strange sound?

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:37.750
Hey! What's that?

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:49.290
Could it be...

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:50.600
Tsukushi!

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:52.660
K-Kazuya! Sakurako!

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:54.600
Oh, no! <i>Nouveau Riche</i>!

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:57.140
Domyoji!

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.070
Let me go!

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:02.570
- What's up with this chick?
- Kazuya, how did you find us?

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:05.010
Your mom told us.

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:07.090
We came on the S.S. Aoike.

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:09.180
It took us two whole days.

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:11.200
Hey, <i>Nouveau Riche</i>!

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.920
Who gave you permission
to come on this island?!

00:16:14.350 --> 00:16:17.170
Well, since they're already here,
it can't be helped.

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:19.190
The more, the merrier.

00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:23.940
Thank you, brothers.

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:25.040
Who are you calling "brother"?

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.200
You bonehead.

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:27.500
Yikes!

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:32.440
It's been a while, Mimisaka, Nishikado.

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:33.910
Ugh.

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:37.220
Wow. She's adorable, like a doll!

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:39.880
Maybe she's a celebrity.

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:42.310
That's right. That's right.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:45.850
It's not surprising that you
think of me that way.

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:48.450
You never learn, do you?

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:52.670
It's so romantic, eating dinner
at poolside.

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:53.660
Yeah!

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:57.390
I'm surprised you didn't
get into an accident...

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:58.240
...in that dinky boat.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:00.200
Yeah, but I'm glad we're here.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:04.470
To be with all of you once again
is like a dream.

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:11.750
By the way, Tsukushi. Big news.

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:12.490
Huh?

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:16.080
Shizuka Todo is in this magazine.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:18.690
Wow! Shizuka is? Let me see!

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:19.580
What are you, stupid?

00:17:19.980 --> 00:17:21.260
It's not unusual to see...

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:23.890
...someone like Shizuka in a magazine.

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:27.200
It's not like that. It says that 
some famous French guy...

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:28.780
...is courting her.

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:29.470
What?

00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:30.460
<i>"Courting"?!</i>

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:32.700
By "courting," do you mean...

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:35.460
No, it has nothing to do with tennis.

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:38.300
Are you serious, <i>Nouveau Riche</i>? 
Let me see.

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:45.850
It says, "Shizuka Todo, daughter
of the owner of Todo Trading...

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:48.020
...was asked to be married by
Jean Paul Mailleur...

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:51.080
...rumored to be the next
presidential candidate."

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:53.010
W-wow... Shizuka's...

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:54.180
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:57.730
Possible marriage by
the end of the year?

00:17:57.730 --> 00:17:58.920
Are you serious?

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:00.590
Rui!

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:01.960
Did you know about this?

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:04.690
I did.

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:07.600
It was the talk of the town while
I was still in Paris.

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:09.950
A-are you okay with it?

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:12.100
Shizuka might get married!

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:14.020
It's okay.

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:16.670
It's over. All of it.

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:21.880
<i>So that's what happened.</i>

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:24.850
<i>We could date on the sly.</i>

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:28.420
<i>The reason he changed so much
after he came home...</i>

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:32.740
I'm just a kid...

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:35.220
...who can't do anything for
the woman I love.

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:40.830
<i>It's because he left alone and hurt.</i>

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:42.900
<i>All for Shizuka...</i>

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:11.650
Makino...

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:15.450
I told you I'm okay.

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:17.650
Go back to your room and
go to sleep.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:22.730
Are you crying?

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:28.130
Why should you cry?

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:32.600
Leave me alone and
go back to Tsukasa.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:34.470
I can't leave you alone.

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:39.710
Even if I try, I can't get you
out of my mind.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:43.590
I can't... I just can't!

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:56.330
Why won't you just be happy?

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:02.000
I can't stop thinking 
about things I shouldn't.

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:21.550
Why didn't I...

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:27.490
fall for a woman like you?

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:11.730
You let your hair down a little

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:19.610
You hid the fact
that you were crying

00:22:21.370 --> 00:22:29.480
I noticed, but I
couldn't ask you why

00:22:29.720 --> 00:22:37.520
I can never be
honest about how I feel

00:22:37.520 --> 00:22:45.300
Until after we've split
up after a bad fight

00:22:45.560 --> 00:22:53.440
I can say it now,
though, over and over

00:22:45.560 --> 00:22:53.440
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:22:53.440 --> 00:23:01.810
I can say "I love you"...

00:22:53.440 --> 00:23:01.810
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:11.590
Do you really hate me this time?

00:23:11.590 --> 00:23:19.360
Will you end up running to him?

00:23:19.630 --> 00:23:27.540
I can say it now,
though, over and over

00:23:19.630 --> 00:23:27.540
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:27.540 --> 00:23:35.950
I can say "I love you"...

00:23:27.540 --> 00:23:35.950
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:49.660 --> 00:23:51.260
Since we got back from our trip...

00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:55.670
...Domyoji's eyes have been so cold,
it's more than I can take.

00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:57.730
